  explanation: "This is the same 6-to-24-month language-ladder question style as `pedep2-nd-9`, but Lizzie's clue is motor rather than language: she has just started crawling. The course's slide-deck milestones place crawling explicitly at 8 months (\"8 months: Crawl\"), and the same deck's gross-motor summary lists crawling across 8–9 months; the milestone table instead groups it into a broader 9–10 month band alongside pulling to stand. The printed key here, B (8 months), matches the earlier, more specific slide figure rather than the table's grouped range — a minor variation between two parts of the same course material rather than a contradiction, and nothing here moves the key. For comparison, `pedep2-nd-9`'s clue on this same ladder, saying a word specific to one person (\"dada\" to her father), is timed two rungs later at 10 months.\n\nWritten for this bank — Pediatrics endpoint part2.pdf prints no explanation here.",
